#EMBEDDED_NOTES
#The effect of the trailer on the car is interpreted by calculating aero coefficients for the combined car with trailer, resolved at the aero reference point of the car. This calculation assumes that the car and trailer are rigidly connected together, which is not true in general (the ball hitch does not transfer moments).
#
#However, vehicles with trailers are tested as a rigid combination in a wind tunnel or CFD simulation on occasion, and similar overall aero coefficients are reported. There does not seem to be a standard choice of frontal area or reference length for this kind of testing. Here we use the values of the car to faciliatate comparison of the combo values with the isolated car values.
#END_EMBEDDED_NOTES

